---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Full-stack developer in Mexico building websites for small businesses and web applications for institutions. Available worldwide in English and Spanish."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="display" style="max-width:16ch">I check my work before I call it done.</h1>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <p>
          Hi, I'm {site.name}. I'm a full-stack developer from {site.location},
          and I work with clients anywhere, in English or Spanish.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most of my background is software for institutions: systems that
          handle anonymous answers and sensitive records. When thousands of
          people trust your system, you learn quickly. Write the plan before
          the code, test every change, and keep an eye on security the whole
          way.
        </p>
        <p>
          I bring the same habits to small-business sites. Does a bakery's
          website need thousands of tests? No. But it does need to work on
          real phones, load fast, say clearly what you sell, and give Google
          clean information. I check all of that before launch.
        </p>
        <h2>What I work with</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> React, TypeScript, and Astro. I use static pages whenever they fit.</li>
          <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Django, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, Redis, Celery.</li>
          <li><strong>Ops:</strong> Docker, AWS (EC2, ECR, SSM), CI/CD pipelines, monitoring.</li>
          <li><strong>Security:</strong> authentication and session reviews.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>How we'd work together</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>A written plan: what I build, when, and for how much.</li>
          <li>A live link every week, so you can click around the real thing.</li>
          <li>Launch with tests, documentation, and monitoring in place.</li>
          <li>Full handover: your code, your hosting, your accounts.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          If that's how you think software should be built,
          <a href="/contact/">let's talk</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
